\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec4 I built a 4-bit ALU in VHDL by connecting four 1-bit ALUs. It handles addition, subtraction, AND/OR operations, and checks for overflow, zero results, and comparisons. The trickiest parts were setting up the carry chain for subtraction and verifying the overflow logic. I worked alone on this, using only class materials, and finished in about 4 hours. This project helped me better understand ALU design and VHDL.}